<Base
  title="Sample bid triage — BidScout"
  description="A real one-page BidScout triage of a live federal roofing solicitation: verdict, scoring, deadlines, gotchas, and next actions."
  canonical="/sample-triage/"
>
  <style>
    .verdict { display: inline-block; font-weight: 700; padding: .15rem .6rem; border-radius: .45rem; background: color-mix(in srgb, #2da44e 18%, transparent); border: 1px solid #2da44e; }
    dl.facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: .25rem .9rem; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: .95rem; }
    dl.facts dt { font-weight: 600; opacity: .75; }
    dl.facts dd { margin: 0; }
    table.score { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: .5rem 0 1rem; font-size: .95rem; }
    table.score td, table.score th { text-align: left; padding: .35rem .5rem; border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 15%, transparent); }
    table.score td:last-child { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    .note { font-size: .85rem; opacity: .7; }
    ol li, ul li { margin: .3rem 0; }
  </style>

  <p class="note">This is a real triage of a live solicitation, exactly as a Triage-tier
  client receives it (one page per bid, scored against <em>their</em> company profile —
  here we assume a small Ohio-area roofing contractor). Prepared 2026-08-23.</p>

  <h1>B101 and B136 Roof Repairs — 180th Fighter Wing</h1>
  <p><span class="verdict">PURSUE · 16/20</span></p>
  <p><strong>Why:</strong> 100% small-business set-aside roof repair with a clear
  two-phase scope, quotes rather than full proposals, and a fast 60-day job.</p>

  <dl class="facts">
    <dt>Buyer</dt><dd>Dept of Defense / Ohio Air National Guard, 180th Fighter Wing (Swanton, OH — Toledo area)</dd>
    <dt>Due</dt><dd>Aug 31, 2026, 10:00 AM ET</dd>
    <dt>Work window</dt><dd>Start within 10 days of notice to proceed; complete within 60 days</dd>
    <dt>Est. value</dt><dd>Not stated (scope suggests low six figures)</dd>
    <dt>Set-aside</dt><dd>100% Small Business — NAICS 238160 (Roofing Contractors)</dd>
    <dt>Notice</dt><dd><a href="https://sam.gov/opp/a4b1b30606614254ae20de9e52822c15/view" rel="nofollow">View on SAM.gov</a></dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>What the job actually is</h2>
  <p>Firm fixed-price commercial construction. <strong>Phase 1</strong> repairs Bldg 101's
  flat/standing-seam roof: eave gutter details, a downspout, curb and sanitary-stack
  re-seals, roughly 1,300 feet of seam repair, and 30 walk mats. <strong>Phase 2</strong>
  decommissions Bldg 136's rooftop solar array — demo the panels, cable tray, and
  electrical back to the inverter — then patches the membrane. All labor, materials,
  equipment, and supervision included.</p>

  <h2>Scoring</h2>
  <table class="score">
    <tr><td>Fit to trade &amp; size — pure roofing repair; set-aside keeps large primes out</td><td>5/5</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Competition pressure — repair scope narrows the field; two amendments show some engagement</td><td>4/5</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Effort to bid — RFQ on SF-1442, Q&amp;A already answered and attached</td><td>4/5</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Margin signal — membrane condition under the solar rows is the unknown</td><td>3/5</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Total</th><th>16/20 → PURSUE</th></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Deadlines &amp; gotchas</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Two amendments</strong> (Aug 6, Aug 17) — your quote must acknowledge both in section 19 or it can be rejected.</li>
    <li>Amendment 2 added clause 52.223-2 (biobased-product reporting) and set the 10-day performance start.</li>
    <li>Davis-Bacon prevailing wages apply — check the attached wage determination before pricing labor.</li>
    <li>SAM.gov registration must be active at time of quote.</li>
    <li>Phase 2 includes electrical demolition — line up a licensed electrician sub if that's not in-house.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>If you pursue: next three actions</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Today:</strong> download the amended package, Q&amp;A, and new SF-1442 from SAM.gov; confirm SAM registration is active.</li>
    <li><strong>By Aug 26:</strong> walk the seam/gutter quantities against the SOW; get an electrician's quote for the Phase 2 demo.</li>
    <li><strong>By Aug 28:</strong> price both phases, complete the SF-1442 acknowledging both amendments in section 19, and submit before the deadline.</li>
  </ol>

  <p class="note">Every claim above is traceable to the public solicitation. Verify dates
  and requirements against the posted documents before bidding.</p>

